INFO  [Claude Code] Perfect! I've successfully resolved the issues preventing test creation for `MarketData` and `MarketReporting`. Here's what I did:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ## Summary
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] Both issues were caused by `UnresolvedAddressException` when Diffblue Cover tried to construct instances of `MarketData` and `MarketReporting` using the `open()` static factory method, which requires real network addresses and connections.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ## Solution
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] I added the `@InterestingTestFactory` annotation to the existing factory methods in `TestFactories.java`:
INFO  [Claude Code] - `createMarketData()` - applications/system/src/test/java/com/paritytrading/parity/system/TestFactories.java:28
INFO  [Claude Code] - `createMarketReporting()` - applications/system/src/test/java/com/paritytrading/parity/system/TestFactories.java:40
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] These factory methods create instances with null network channels, which is acceptable for unit testing and avoids the network-related exceptions.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ## How This Works
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The `@InterestingTestFactory` annotation tells Diffblue Cover to use these factory methods instead of trying to construct instances through the problematic `open()` method that requires:
INFO  [Claude Code] - Valid network interfaces
INFO  [Claude Code] - Resolved multicast addresses  
INFO  [Claude Code] - Bound request addresses
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] This pattern was already successfully used in the same file for other factory methods like `createOrderEntryWithChannel()` and `createSessionWithTransport()`.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The Maven build completed successfully with all modules building without errors, confirming that the changes are valid and the classpath is properly updated.
